//@ compile-fail
//@ error-pattern: error[E001]
//@ error-pattern: expected f32
//@ description: PR #1737 w12 -- only LITERALS coerce to f32, never a non-literal f64
// Regression port of tests/witness_matrix/cases/w12_nonliteral_must_reject.sio
// into the standard suite.
//
// CARDINAL NEGATIVE for the f32 lane: the literal-coercion fix (w11) lets a
// float LITERAL adopt f32 from context (`let x: f32 = 1.5`). The cardinal rule
// it must not break: only literals coerce. A non-literal f64 value carries a
// real type and must still be REJECTED -- narrowing it silently would be a
// precision decision made behind the user's back, the exact thing the
// magnitude-guard design (w13) exists to prevent. Converting is what the
// explicit `as f32` cast is for (see f32_cast_no_real_narrowing_residual.sio
// for what that cast currently does and does not do).
//
// Measured 2026-08-16 on a fresh source build of main @ a5548481d1:
// rejected, error[E001] "this binding expects a different type ... expected
// f32", no ELF emitted. Under the pre-fix Jul-25 prebuilt this was also
// rejected -- the witness guards against the coercion ever being widened,
// not against a live defect.

fn main() -> i64 {
    let big: f64 = 1.5
    let x: f32 = big
    0
}
